# armour/motif/woman/straps: the chest motif STRAPS (STYLE_P2 28.3 "chest motif"; contracts 3c.1 `overlay motif.<v>`).
# STRAPS (value key: dark-mid): a leather saltire, 2 px straps from both shoulders crossing on a bright buckle (G), the plate between.
# FORGE-TORSO round 2 i3 (generated from the area src/motifs.py; edit there). Laid on the armour torso at torso z 3,
# anchor neck: the rest view per facing serves every torso key by the key fallback (clipped to that key's torso);
# own views where the fallback misreads. 2-4 px planes lit from the top-left, below the collar's two rows.
# Regions: R its rim (T3 brass, T5 gold), P its plates (T4 etching), G its socket (the T5 gem), N its joins (T6 runes,
# the glowing tell). (i3) Each motif is its own arrangement of light over the whole chest (a gradient, a boss, stripes,
# a V, a split, an X, a yoke, rays) in the full ramp, so it reads at true 1x and in greyscale; the run views go to the key fallback (D21).
# Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
body woman
role overlay motif.straps
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso
z 3
tags overlay

